	(text "PORTS\nJ801 UART sensor port: UART2 = GPIO17 TX (3.3 V out via R801 100R) / GPIO16 RX via U801 74LVC1G17 (5 V-tolerant input,\nR802 keeps it idle-high); pin 1 = 5 V, 200 mA via F801 polyfuse. U802 SRV05-4 = ESD on the four external UART/GPS lines.\nJ802 GPS card header for u-blox type modules: UART on GPIO36 (GPS TX) / GPIO32 (GPS RX), PPS on GPIO39, 100R series.\nR806 holds GPS_TXD high with no module fitted (GPIO36 is input-only, no internal pull-up); R807 holds PPS low.\nGPS supply = 3V3 by default (JP801 bridged 1-2); cut 1-2 and bridge 2-3 for a 5 V module, fused by F803 (200 mA).\nu-blox modules with I2C can use the Qwiic port J803 (address 0x42) instead.\nJ804 expansion: pin 2 = 5 V via F802 (200 mA). IO5 and IO15 are strapping pins - do not pull them low at boot.\nThe port data lines are 3.3/5 V logic: they survive ESD, not a wire to the vehicle supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
